  "title": "Megan The Stallion Receives Writing Credit On Rich Flex Feat On Her Loss Same Project She Received Diss On Circo Loco?",
  "htmlContent": "<!-- wp:image {\"id\":519805,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img src=\"http://landonbuford.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/Megan-Thee-Stallion-and-Drake-696x442-1.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-519805\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"><em>Megan Thee Stallion &amp; Drake. Credit: Taylor Hill/Getty Images for ABA; Joseph Okpako/WireImage</em></figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Megan Thee Stallion got a writing credit on Drake and the new 21 Savage album, Her Loss. On Friday (Nov. 4), the credit list for Drake and 21 Savage's Her Loss album unveiled that despite not being featured on any of the songs, Megan Thee Stallion earned credit from the writer on the joint project.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Soon after Megan Thee Stallion responded to Drake for his alleged diss of Meg on the song,\"Circo Loco,\" detectives of the music industry discovered the fact that underneath her government name, Megan Pete, the Houston rapper is, in fact, noted as having contributed to the introduction song of the new album, \"Rich Flex.\"</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KDr5eUFHyW8\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KDr5eUFHyW8\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Megan being credited as one of the writers on \"Rich Flex\" is apparently the result of a 21 Savage rhyme footage.<br>raps on a song that is considered an interpolation from Meg 2020 single, \"Savage.\"</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In a certain section of the first verse of the song, 21 references himself using the exact cadence and flow that Megan uses as a refrain about her multi-platinum hit.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>\"I'm a savage,\" raps&nbsp;21 Savage.&nbsp;\"Smack her booty in Magic/I'll slap a p**** n*** with a ratchet.\"</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><br>In the early hours of Friday morning, the Internet started buzzing around Drake's apparent accusation that Megan lied. about allegedly getting shot by Tory Lanez in 2020 <a href=\"https://landonbuford.com/2022/11/04/megan-thee-stallion-slams-drake-for-his-lyrics-referencing-her-shooting-on-circo-loco-with-21-savage/\">on the song \"Circo Loco.\"</a><br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In response, the Hot Girl Summer artist hit Twitter with a long tirade, seemingly implying that Drake is corny for using her shooting for clout.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Stallion writing credit on Rich Flex can be seen below:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":519801,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img src=\"http://landonbuford.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/attachment-megan-thee-stallion-drake-21-savage-writing-credit-rich-flex.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-519801\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"><a href=\"data:image/png;base64,\">XXL.Com</a></figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
